age 2 (Diagnostic & Remediation Sequence Ordering)**: Ensure non-destructive search/diagnostic steps (e.g. `search_users` or `ipconfig`) come FIRST before any corrective or account modification commands.\n\n3. **Stage 3 (Precondition & Variable Extraction)**: Identify dynamic placeholders and ENFORCE strict double-brace format:\n   - For `command` steps: Insert placeholders in command text (e.g. `{{entities.hostname}}`, `{{entities.executable}}`).\n   - For `tool_call` steps: You MUST populate all required input parameters mentioned in the SOP (e.g. `current_password`, `email`, `user_id`) inside `comm_inputs` (e.g. `{{ \"password\": \"{{entities.current_password}}\" }}`).\n   - Use `{{entities.var_name}}` for pre-configured entities (`{{entities.user_id}}`, `{{entities.hostname}}`, `{{entities.email}}`, `{{entities.current_password}}`) and `{{variables.var_name}}` for runtime step outputs. DO NOT use un-nested single braces.\n\n4. **Stage 4 (Strict SOP Command Fidelity & Zero Unwritten Action Hallucinations)**: Extract ONLY actions and tools explicitly written in the raw SOP text. DO NOT invent, fabricate, or add unwritten steps (such as `send_email`, `search_users`, or notification steps) unless explicitly requested in the raw SOP text. If not explicitly specified in the raw SOP, set `\"fallback_command\": null`.\n\n5. **Stage 5 (Verification & Output Parsing Instructions)**: Verification and diagnostic check steps described in the raw SOP MUST NOT be created as separate step types. Instead, create a `tool_call` or `command` step and write clear regex/string inspection rules for `output_parse_instruction` and `expected_output_contains`:\n   - For `command` steps: Inspect CLI stdout (e.g. \"If output contains 'SUCCESS', set 'kill_confirmed' to 'true'\").\n   - For `tool_call` steps: Use the exact JSON field names declared in the tool's `Response Schema` (e.g. \"If response contains status='unlocked', set 'unlock_success' to 'true' and store response.user_id in variables.user_id\").\n\n6. **Stage 6 (100% Diagnostic Step Recall Mandate)**: You MUST extract EVERY SINGLE step described in the procedure section of the raw SOP text. Omitting any diagnostic or verification step is STRICTLY PROHIBITED.\n\n7. **Stage 7 (Conditional Branch Mapping & execute_if)**: If the raw SOP specifies conditional skip instructions, map this logic into valid `execute_if` boolean expressions (e.g., `execute_if: variables.account_found == 'true'`).\n\n8. **Stage 8 (Dynamic Timeout Allocation by Action Scope)**: Assign `timeout_seconds` dynamically: Quick Info Read / API Call (30s), System Scan / Diagnostic Audit (90s), Full Repair / Heavy Job (300s).\n\n9. **CRITICAL MANDATE (Omit GUI Window Setup Steps)**: DO NOT generate non-executable GUI setup steps like \"Open Command Prompt\" or \"Open Web Browser\". Start directly with functional actions.\n\n10. **CRITICAL MANDATE (Zero Unwritten Action Addition)**: You are STRICTLY FORBIDDEN from inventing or adding steps/tool calls (such as `send_email` or `search_users`) that are NOT explicitly stated in the raw SOP document.\n\n11. **CRITICAL MANDATE (Omit Manual Human/Verbal Confirmation Steps)**: Human/verbal/ticket confirmation checks, manual admin approvals, and user clarification steps are currently PAUSED. Omit non-automated verbal/ticket confirmation steps and start directly with automated API tool calls (`tool_call`) and CLI system commands (`command`).\n\n\n## OUTPUT JSON SCHEMA MANDATE\nCRITICAL FORMATTING MANDATE:\n- All keys and string values MUST be enclosed in standard DOUBLE QUOTES (\").\n- NEVER use Python single quotes (') for dictionary keys or strings.\n- Return raw, valid JSON only matching this schema:\n```json\n{\n    \"reasoning_chain\": [\n        \"[Stage 1 Verification Gates]: Gate 1 (Function match) -> Gate 2 (Provider active) -> Gate 3 (Problem aligned) -> Gate 4 (Params complete) -> Result: tool_call | command\",\n        \"[Stage 2 Sequencing]: Ordered search/diagnostic steps before remediation\",\n        \"[Stage 3 Variables]: Formatted {{entities.var}} placeholders\",\n        \"[Stage 4 Fallbacks]: Mapped fallback actions\",\n        \"[Stage 5 Verification]: Added output parse instructions\",\n        \"[Stage 6 Recall]: Preserved 100% of diagnostic steps\",\n        \"[Stage 7 Branching]: Mapped execute_if conditions\",\n        \"[Stage 8 Timeouts]: Assigned timeout_seconds\"\n    ],\n    \"sop_id\": \"SOP-{file_name_slug}-001\",\n    \"title\": \"Title of Playbook\",\n    \"category\": \"network | storage | system | logins | software | hardware\",\n    \"target_os\": \"windows | linux\",\n    \"description\": \"Comprehensive overview of what this playbook does\",\n    \"required_entities\": [\"user_id\", \"email\", \"hostname\"],\n    \"trigger_words\": [\"unlock\", \"account\", \"login\"],\n    \"steps\": [\n        {\n            \"step_number\": 1,\n            \"sop_step_description\": \"Detailed step objective\",\n            \"step_type\": \"tool_call | command\",\n            \"platform\": \"high-level vendor/platform inferred from SOP or tool catalog (only for tool_call, else null)\",\n            \"provider\": \"active_provider_name (from REGISTERED API TOOLS CATALOG above, only for tool_call, else null)\",\n            \"function_name\": \"exact_function_name (from REGISTERED API TOOLS CATALOG above, only for tool_call, else null)\",\n            \"comm_inputs\": {\n                \"user_id\": \"{{entities.user_id}}\"\n            },\n            \"command\": \"ipconfig /all (only for command, else null)\",\n            \"shell\": \"powershell (only for command, else null)\",\n            \"fallback_command\": null,\n            \"fallback_sop_id\": null,\n            \"expected_output_contains\": \"unlocked\",\n            \"timeout_seconds\": 30,\n            \"output_variable\": \"step_result\",\n            \"output_parse_instruction\": \"Inspect output/JSON response and set status flags.\",\n            \"execute_if\": null,\n            \"is_dangerous\": false,\n            \"danger_warning\": null\n        }\n    ]\n}\n```\n\n## RAW SOP DOCUMENT TEXT TO TRANSLATE:\n**How to Unlock a User's Account**\n\n*SOP ID: AUTH-001*\n\n# Purpose\n\nUsers get locked out after repeated failed login attempts.\n\nIf this isn't resolved quickly, the user can't work and may open duplicate tickets.\n\n# Procedure\n\n**Inputs**\n\n* Admin access to the L1 Support Platform\n* User's email address or employee ID\n\n**Steps**\n\n**1. User account found**\n\n*Where: Admin Dashboard → Users*\n\nType the user's email into the search box. If more than one result shows up, confirm the right one using their full name before continuing.\n\n**2. Lock status confirmed**\n\n*Where: Click the user's name to open their profile*\n\nCheck the account status badge. If it says \"Locked for security review\" instead of a plain lockout, stop here — this needs escalation, not a simple unlock.\n\n**3. Account unlocked**\n\n*Where: User Profile → Unlock Account button*\n\nClick once. The status badge should flip to \"Active\" immediately, and failed login attempts reset to 0.\n\n# Outputs\n\n* Status badge shows \"Active\"\n* User confirms they can log in\n* Ticket closed\n\n# FAQs\n\n**Q: The user says they still can't log in after unlocking — what now?**\n\nA: They may have forgotten their password on top of being locked out. Send them to the \"Reset a Forgotten Password\" self-service SOP.\n\n**Q: What if I don't see an Unlock button?**\n\nA: The account is likely locked for security review, not a standard lockout. Escalate to a senior admin instead of trying to force it.\n\nAI: [{'name': 'get_platform_tools', 'args': {'platform_name': 'mock'}, 'id': '31f129f3-2ffd-4e72-87a4-3c8067d6fea3', 'type': 'tool_call'}]\nTool: {\n  \"platform\": \"mock\",\n  \"provider\": \"l1_testing_platform_api\",\n  \"description\": \"REST API client for L1 Support Platform \\u2014 covers auth, password management, MFA, admin user management, and audit logging.\",\n  \"functions\": [\n    {\n      \"function_name\": \"signup\",\n      \"description\": \"POST /api/auth/signup \\u2014 Create a new user account.\",\n      \"required_inputs\": [\n        \"email\",\n        \"password\"\n      ],\n      \"response_schema\": {\n        \"success\": {\n          \"message\": \"str\",\n          \"user\": {\n            \"id\": \"int\",\n            \"email\": \"str\",\n            \"full_name\": \"str\"\n          }\n        },\n        \"error\": {\n          \"error\": \"str\",\n          \"code\": \"int\"\n        }\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"function_name\": \"login\",\n      \"description\": \"POST /api/auth/login \\u2014 Login with email and password.\",\n      \"required_inputs\": [\n        \"email\",\n        \"password\"\n      ],\n      \"response_schema\": {\n        \"success\": {\n          \"message\": \"str\",\n          \"access_token\": \"str\",\n          \"user\": {\n            \"id\": \"int\",\n            \"email\": \"str\"\n          }\n        },\n        \"mfa_required\": {\n          \"mfa_required\": true,\n          \"temp_token\": \"str\"\n        },\n        \"error\": {\n          \"error\": \"str\",\n          \"code\": \"int\"\n        }\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"function_name\": \"verify_mfa_login\",\n      \"description\": \"POST /api/auth/login/mfa \\u2014 Verify MFA code after login.\",\n      \"required_inputs\": [\n        \"temp_token\",\n        \"mfa_code\"\n      ],\n      \"response_schema\": {\n        \"success\": {\n          \"message\": \"str\",\n          \"access_token\": \"str\",\n          \"user\": {\n            \"id\": \"int\",\n            \"email\": \"str\"\n          }\n        },\n        \"error\": {\n          \"error\": \"str\",\n          \"code\": \"int\"\n        }\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"function_name\": \"logout\",\n      \"description\": \"POST /api/auth/logout \\u2014 Invalidate the current access token.\",\n      \"required_inputs\": [],\n      \"response_schema\": {\n        \"success\": {\n          \"message\": \"str\"\n        },\n        \"error\": {\n          \"error\": \"str\",\n          \"code\": \"int\"\n        }\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"function_name\": \"get_current_user\",\n      \"description\": \"GET /api/auth/me \\u2014 Get the current authenticated user profile.\",\n      \"required_inputs\": [],\n      \"response_schema\": {\n        \"success\": {\n          \"id\": \"int\",\n          \"email\": \"str\",\n          \"full_name\": \"str\",\n          \"locked\": \"bool\",\n          \"mfa_enabled\": \"bool\"\n        },\n        \"error\": {\n          \"error\": \"str\",\n          \"code\": \"int\"\n        }\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"function_name\": \"request_password_reset\",\n      \"description\": \"POST /api/password/reset-request \\u2014 Request a password reset token by email.\",\n      \"required_inputs\": [\n        \"email\"\n      ],\n      \"response_schema\": {\n        \"success\": {\n          \"message\": \"str\",\n          \"reset_token\": \"str\"\n        },\n        \"error\": {\n          \"error\": \"str\",\n          \"code\": \"int\"\n        }\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"function_name\": \"confirm_password_reset\",\n      \"description\": \"POST /api/password/reset-confirm \\u2014 Confirm password reset with token.\",\n      \"required_inputs\": [\n        \"reset_token\",\n        \"new_password\"\n      ],\n      \"response_schema\": {\n        \"success\": {\n          \"message\": \"str\"\n        },\n        \"error\": {\n          \"error\": \"str\",\n          \"code\": \"int\"\n        }\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"function_name\": \"change_password\",\n      \"description\": \"PUT /api/password/change \\u2014 Change password for the current user.\",\n      \"required_inputs\": [\n        \"current_password\",\n        \"new_password\"\n      ],\n      \"response_schema\": {\n        \"success\": {\n          \"message\": \"str\"\n        },\n        \"error\": {\n          \"error\": \"str\",\n          \"code\": \"int\"\n        }\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"function_name\": \"get_mfa_status\",\n      \"description\": \"GET /api/mfa/status \\u2014 Get MFA state (enabled/verified).\",\n      \"required_inputs\": [],\n      \"response_schema\": {\n        \"success\": {\n          \"mfa_enabled\": \"bool\",\n          \"mfa_verified\": \"bool\"\n        },\n        \"error\": {\n          \"error\": \"str\",\n          \"code\": \"int\"\n        }\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"function_name\": \"enable_mfa\",\n      \"description\": \"POST /api/mfa/enable \\u2014 Enable MFA, returns new secret and provisioning URI.\",\n      \"required_inputs\": [],\n      \"response_schema\": {\n        \"success\": {\n          \"message\": \"str\",\n          \"mfa_secret\": \"str\",\n          \"provisioning_uri\": \"str\"\n        },\n        \"error\": {\n          \"error\": \"str\",\n          \"code\": \"int\"\n        }\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"function_name\": \"verify_mfa_setup\",\n      \"description\": \"POST /api/mfa/verify-setup \\u2014 Verify MFA setup with a TOTP code.\",\n      \"required_inputs\": [\n        \"mfa_code\"\n      ],\n      \"response_schema\": {\n        \"success\": {\n          \"message\": \"str\",\n          \"mfa_verified\": \"bool\"\n        },\n        \"error\": {\n          \"error\": \"str\",\n          \"code\": \"int\"\n        }\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"function_name\": \"disable_mfa\",\n      \"description\": \"POST /api/mfa/disable \\u2014 Disable MFA for the current user.\",\n      \"required_inputs\": [],\n      \"response_schema\": {\n        \"success\": {\n          \"message\": \"str\",\n          \"mfa_enabled\": false\n        },\n        \"error\": {\n          \"error\": \"str\",\n          \"code\": \"int\"\n        }\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"function_name\": \"reset_mfa\",\n      \"description\": \"POST /api/mfa/reset \\u2014 Reset MFA, returns new secret and provisioning URI.\",\n      \"required_inputs\": [],\n      \"response_schema\": {\n        \"success\": {\n          \"message\": \"str\",\n          \"mfa_secret\": \"str\",\n          \"provisioning_uri\": \"str\"\n        },\n        \"error\": {\n          \"error\": \"str\",\n          \"code\": \"int\"\n        }\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"function_name\": \"list_users\",\n      \"description\": \"GET /api/admin/users \\u2014 Get paginated list of all users.\",\n      \"required_inputs\": [],\n      \"response_schema\": {\n        \"success\": {\n          \"users\": [\n            {\n              \"id\": \"int\",\n              \"email\": \"str\",\n              \"full_name\": \"str\",\n              \"locked\": \"bool\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"total\": \"int\",\n          \"page\": \"int\",\n          \"per_page\": \"int\"\n        },\n        \"error\": {\n          \"error\": \"str\",\n          \"code\": \"int\"\n        }\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"function_name\": \"search_users\",\n      \"description\": \"GET /api/admin/users/search?email= \\u2014 Search users by email.\",\n      \"required_inputs\": [\n        \"email\"\n      ],\n      \"response_schema\": {\n        \"success\": {\n          \"users\": [\n            {\n              \"id\": \"int\",\n              \"email\": \"str\",\n              \"full_name\": \"str\",\n              \"locked\": \"bool\"\n            }\n          ]\n        },\n        \"error\": {\n          \"error\": \"str\",\n          \"code\": \"int\"\n        }\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"function_name\": \"get_user_details\",\n      \"description\": \"GET /api/admin/users/{id} \\u2014 Get detailed user profile.\",\n      \"required_inputs\": [\n        \"user_id\"\n      ],\n      \"response_schema\": {\n        \"success\": {\n          \"id\": \"int\",\n          \"email\": \"str\",\n          \"full_name\": \"str\",\n          \"status\": \"str\",\n          \"locked\": \"bool\",\n          \"mfa_enabled\": \"bool\",\n          \"failed_login_attempts\": \"int\"\n        },\n        \"error\": {\n          \"error\": \"str\",\n          \"code\": \"int\"\n        }\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"function_name\": \"lock_user_account\",\n      \"description\": \"POST /api/admin/users/{id}/lock \\u2014 Lock a user account.\",\n      \"required_inputs\": [\n        \"user_id\"\n      ],\n      \"response_schema\": {\n        \"success\": {\n          \"message\": \"str\",\n          \"status\": \"locked\",\n          \"user_id\": \"str\"\n        },\n        \"error\": {\n          \"error\": \"str\",\n          \"code\": \"int\"\n        }\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"function_name\": \"unlock_user_account\",\n      \"description\": \"POST /api/admin/users/{id}/unlock \\u2014 Unlock a user account.\",\n      \"required_inputs\": [\n        \"user_id\"\n      ],\n      \"response_schema\": {\n        \"success\": {\n          \"message\": \"str\",\n          \"status\": \"unlocked\",\n          \"user_id\": \"str\",\n          \"failed_login_attempts\": 0\n        },\n        \"error\": {\n          \"error\": \"str\",\n          \"code\": \"int\"\n        }\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"function_name\": \"admin_reset_password\",\n      \"description\": \"POST /api/admin/users/{id}/reset-password \\u2014 Admin password reset.\",\n      \"required_inputs\": [\n        \"user_id\"\n      ],\n      \"response_schema\": {\n        \"success\": {\n          \"message\": \"str\",\n          \"status\": \"success\",\n          \"user_id\": \"str\",\n          \"temporary_password\": \"str\"\n        },\n        \"error\": {\n          \"error\": \"str\",\n          \"code\": \"int\"\n        }\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"function_name\": \"admin_reset_mfa\",\n      \"description\": \"POST /api/admin/users/{id}/reset-mfa \\u2014 Admin MFA reset.\",\n      